{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\nClosing satiated-unrideable-tapeworm (Gerrit 1809, merged 42cd70b889) left three residual sub-clauses that are test/reporting hardening, not behavior gaps — all behavior is merged, tested observable-behaviour-style, and CI-green. This ticket carries the remainder so the parent could close honestly.\n\n## Scope (from the parent's AC1-AC3 residuals; full tables in the parent's close-out comment)\n1. AC1 residual: add call-count/monkeypatch assertions on the shared confirmation reduce path so a future regression that bypasses the shared seam (printing per-verb again) is caught structurally, not just per-verb by exact-line tests.\n2. AC2 residual: ship the verb inventory table (no-op-capable vs always-writes) as generated or hand-maintained documentation (docs/cli-reference or a test-enforced table), so the no-op contract is enumerable.\n3. AC3 residual: record the per-verb old→new confirmation-line mapping (the parent's comment has the full table) in docs or the test suite as golden data.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] Reduce-path structural assertion exists (call-count or seam-spy) covering at least create/link/transition. — seam-spy on `_confirm.emit`/`emit_text` in `tests/unit/test_mutation_confirmations.py`: parametrized over create/link/transition, asserts exactly ONE routed line and `stdout == routed_line + newline`; plus a no-op variant (re-link, already-at-status transition). Proven to bite by mutation (replacing `confirm_created`'s `emit_text` with `print` fails it). `test_confirmation_formatters_need_no_store` proves the line needs no store read.\n- [x] Verb inventory (no-op-capable vs always-writes) lives in a durable, reviewable location and a test fails when a verb is added without classification. — `MUTATION_VERBS` in `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` (17 rows = `_WRITES_FULL | _LIFECYCLE`), rendered as the 'Verb inventory' table in the generated `docs/cli-reference.md`; `_check_mutation_verbs()` makes `render()` raise on drift from `rebar._cli._CONFIRM_SCOPE` (CI drift gate fails), and `test_an_unclassified_verb_fails_the_generator` asserts that directly.\n- [x] Old→new mapping table recorded in docs or golden test data. — the 'Confirmation-line record (pre-`42cd70b889` → today)' table in `docs/cli-reference.md`, sourced from the same curated rows; old strings read out of `42cd70b889^` rather than paraphrased.\n- [x] make lint / make typecheck clean; lands via Gerrit. — lint PASS (complexity active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0), typecheck PASS (572 files), full `tests/unit` 5077 passed. Gerrit 1933 merged as `0c1906abc9` with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, 0 unresolved."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787190130697854001,"uuid":"9eb34681-0a98-4ab1-b79f-7d61a2b88018"}